        "section": [
          {
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">COPD exacerbation, treated with bronchodilators and steroids</div>"
            },
            "code": {
              "coding": [
                {
                  "code": "67781-5",
                  "system": "http://loinc.org",
                  "display": "Summarization of encounter note"
                }
              ]
            },
            "title": "Synthesis"
          },
          {
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">Dear colleague, I am writing to inform you about the hospital course of your patient, a 65-year-old female admitted on 20/09/2023 with an acute exacerbation of known chronic obstructive pulmonary disease. On admission, she presented with increased dyspnoea, productive cough, and reduced oxygen saturation. Chest X-ray confirmed hyperinflation without evidence of pneumonia or pneumothorax. Arterial blood gas analysis revealed hypoxaemia with mild hypercapnia. Blood tests showed a mild inflammatory response. She was treated with nebulised bronchodilators, systemic corticosteroids, supplemental oxygen therapy, and received patient education regarding inhaler technique and exacerbation management. She responded well to treatment with significant clinical improvement. She is discharged in stable condition and I recommend close follow-up and continuation of her optimised inhaler regimen.</div>"
            },
            "code": {
              "coding": [
